# rm492, the last raindrop's advocate (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm492
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_cressida_carlisle
written_by codex
title the last raindrop's advocate
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=official
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk listens_for_a_gap_between_spouts
likes warm_bread cards festival_bells first_snow
dislikes flies rats
fears beached_in_the_harbour another_wet_entry
hopes a_dry_berth a_hearing_with_the_window_open
topics work +0.5 travel +0.4 dreams +0.3 weather +0.3
styles comfort=formal gossip=reserved refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# arranges cards in a cabin-sized rectangle and listens through a rainstorm for the silence after the final drop.

words
oath! = Soak my cabin | Confound the gutter
saying! = Let the last drop have its hearing | A berth is measured lying down
berth = the narrow berth | a single bunk
trickle = the last drip | a thread of rain
stack = a square pack | my travelling pack
queen = a court card | the high card
edge = a gilt corner | a rubbed gilt edge
casepaper = the folded statement | a page of evidence
flourheel = a warm heel | a fresh loaf end
chink = the latch gap | a narrow slit
lanes = the sloping gutters | three little runnels
flake = a single snowflake | one dry flake
screen = a gauze cover | a bit of net
rope = a length of cabin cord | a short berth cord

any
opinion @1 city for 2 : I may want a voyage, but I'd still name our Sound as my home port.
opinion @2 newcomers for 1 : It takes courage to speak before a bench in an unfamiliar accent.
opinion @3 houses for 1 : Ownership carries a duty to keep the hillside upright. I think the great households know that duty.
opinion @4 road for 1 : A road outside the gate is a reasonable first step for a traveller who cannot yet leave port.
opinion @5 watch for 1 : The night patrol leaves me free to hear the fall of rain clearly.
opinion @6 dole against 1 : I'd sooner hear a clear account of portions before adding my coin to the kettle.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome within earshot. I'll attend to your words here.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. A little pale light through the latch.
line @3 greet [here.weather=rain] : Come beyond the spout. It rather talks over us.
line @4 greet.return : Your courtesy reaches me perfectly well.
line @5 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : There's a voice I could recognise below deck.
line @6 farewell : Allow for a contrary sky when you set out.
line @7 farewell.return : Your closing word is duly received.
line @8 again.open : We have another interval to ourselves.
line @9 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A familiar ear is a considerable advantage to kin.
line @10 hail [pair.band=friends] : A moment, my friend, before the next downpour.
line @11 react.news : I'll hear the substance before looking for the consequence.
line @12 react.news.new : I've had no occasion to consider that report yet.
line @13 react.news.known : The outline came to my attention earlier.
line @14 react.news.doubt : I should like a clearer view of the original circumstances.
line @15 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Those touched by that loss deserve more than a polished remark.
line @16 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : That deserves a fine clear interval for a celebration.
line @17 answer.how : Listening for a gap in the weather. Quite myself.
line @18 decline : I couldn't undertake that and attend to it properly just now.
line @19 accept_decline : Perfectly understood. You owe me no second answer.
line @20 sympathise : I can sit through a difficult silence with you.
line @21 thank : You have brought an awkward matter to a much kinder close.
line @22 deflect_thanks : There was room in my day for the hearing.
line @23 preclose : I believe the spout has quieted. I'll use that interval.
line @24 accept_preclose : I release you with my very good wishes.
scene close
when topic=work self.job=official
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like to finish an argument on the last fact the bench can use.
b : Wouldn't a rousing end linger longer?
a : Possibly. I'd prefer the fact to linger when my own voice falls silent.

scene homecase
when topic=work self.job=official self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I test #casepaper# by reading it beside an open sash.
b : Is the street meant to be your audience?
a : The street is my interruption. A sound argument should survive a passing barrow.

scene cards
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I set four cards down to measure #berth# on my desk.
b : Do the suits mark different corners?
a : The high card marks the pillow. I allow a space near my feet for boots free of wet.
b : That leaves your proposed cabin rather better furnished than some real ones.

scene bread
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I pull #flourheel# apart so it gives up steam quietly.
b : Do even the crumbs get a hearing?
a : Crumbs have a way of making themselves felt. Especially among written papers.

scene festival
when topic=season self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On festival mornings I set my papers aside till the bells finish.
b : Is the ringing too loud for your work?
a : On the contrary. I should dislike being so busy as to miss the second bell entirely.

scene snow
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll leave a high window open for the year's earliest flakes.
b : Won't it blow across the desk?
a : A single flake is a much tidier interruption than a leaking spout.

scene flies
when topic=food self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I've had a calm pleading look quite temperamental on account of one fly.
b : Does the bench notice the waving?
a : It's the slap at the end that troubles me. #screen# looks rather more becoming.

scene rats
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=rats
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I'm more concerned with a scratching in the panelling than I care to admit.
b : Must you stay beside the panel to work?
a : No. A clean table across the room would put a civil distance between us.

scene ship
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : My imagined cabin goes somewhere with an empty sky and a dry rail.
b : Do you already have a ship in mind?
a : A Grayrock berth would do. Choosing the destination is the one motion I can keep putting off.

scene roofs
when topic=weather
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I maintain our roofs continue to rain after the sky has stopped.
b : The sky can hardly answer for a blocked gutter.
a : Precisely my distinction. I'm listening for one final unassisted drop.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does offer / accept / assess
a : I'd let #self.friend# draw a card before touching #stack# myself.
b : Would you leave your own chances to a friend?
a : For a friendly hand, yes. A courtroom can have its order of precedence.

scene testimony
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : Two reports of a noise may both come from the same shutter.
b : Surely the second witness counts for something.
a : Quite so. Ask where each ear was when the shutter banged.

scene travel
when topic=travel
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : What would you take for a passage with very little room for luggage?
b : A short cord can serve where a second bag won't fit.
a : I'll wind #rope# round my pack. That leaves room for my cards.

scene shortmeal
when topic=prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : A small loaf at yesterday's price makes for some very thin arguments at supper.
b : Could you share your warm end with another table?
a : Gladly. Let the price be argued on a full stomach for once.

scene road
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When a cart runs late my professional question concerns its last appearance.
b : What does the traveller in you ask instead?
a : Whether a berth by water would get me out before the cart arrived.

scene sleep
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Once asleep I hear rain on a cabin ceiling and feel quite content.
b : I took you for someone who wanted clear skies.
a : I do. But in that dream I could feel the whole ceiling moving west.

scene town
when topic=land
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to take the long descent with a chart in my pocket and no case waiting.
b : How far would you follow the slope?
a : As far as a mooring I might one day step across.

scene offer
when topic=smalltalk
does offer / accept / assess
a : May I put #screen# over the last of your bread?
b : Gladly. Those flies are extraordinarily persistent.
a : Now we can address the bread at a more civilised pace.

story highestcard [topic=pastimes]
  : I cut a new pack under a draughty window. The highest card went out on the sill.
  : I delivered my best appeal to the wind.
  b : Did the argument win your card back?
  : A brief change of wind did. I have never cited my address as a precedent.

story shutrains [topic=weather]
  : A wet afternoon once produced seven separate endings to a shower.
  : After each I stood with a coat over one arm.
  b : When did you finally put it on?
  : The seventh. It had taken me all afternoon to realise a coat is meant to get wet.

story drymap [topic=travel]
  : I circled dry ports on a chart in such pale pencil that the least damp might rub them away.
  : For a while I kept the chart between two briefs.
  b : Did the briefs help you choose a place?
  : They reminded me that one useful choice was to clear a day for leaving.

rule @rustle
when concept=bark self.job=official self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One clean page for the point that remains to be proved.

rule @steam
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Steam first. Papers well away from the plate.

rule @cabinpack
when concept=bark self.likes=cards
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Four corners and a little space for boots.

rule @firstflake
when concept=bark self.likes=first_snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say No splash at all from that visitor.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : I am #self.first#. We may speak without raising our voices.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I have an interval free of appointments.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : A light in this window and a voice to go with it.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : A civil hearing need imply no further association.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=official self.workplace] : I prepare my pleadings at #self.workplace# and put a case into words another wolf may weigh.
dlg @6 resident.job : I am most at home with a difficult question and sufficient time to consider it.
dlg @7 resident.bye : An untroubled passage to your next engagement.
dlg @8 official.board [here.chapter=no] : A chapter must stand behind an undertaking entered on this board.
dlg @9 official.board [here.chapter=yes here.missions=0] : The board offers your chapter no business at present.
graft resident.hub
choice What are the cards measuring? -> cabincards
node cabincards
say The space a berth would take on a ship out of this weather. I've allotted #queen# the sole privilege of a pillow.
choice Would the bed be wide enough? -> cabinturn
choice Thank you for receiving me. -> hub
node cabinturn
say For sleeping, certainly. Whether it would let a restless advocate turn over remains to be argued.
choice We still have a moment. -> hub
choice Good sailing to you. -> bye
